  "info": {
    "lines": [
      "See: <a href=\"help.html#runningSongFromLibrary\">Tips for running from the Song Library</a><br>",
      "<br>In this song, we are running three plugins simultaneously: <b>fill</b> reads from the Chart and places SingleNotes for the Chart mode (Scale), <b>arpeggio</b> looks at NamedNotes in the Song which are Chart chords and arpeggiates, and <b>transpose</b> goes up chromatically, on every Song-loop. (Note: 6add9 is exactly major pentatonic, so you won't see extra scale notes for that chord.)",
      "<br>",
      "<br>",
      "So you can use this song for both Chord practice and Mode practice.  Play with the show/hide options per note type in View, and save those DisplayOptions in the first Section.  You can either make SingleNotes hidden, or you can turn off FillPlugin with  <menu> /fpfE <i> <b> E</b>nable </i></menu>, and clear its notes with <menu> /fpfC <i> <b> C</b>lear </i></menu>",
      "<br>",
      "<br>",
      "To be able to reset both the transposition and the arpeggio positions at once, map spacebar to \"Reset song hard\" with <menu> /fmZ <i> <b> Z </b> reset song hard </i></menu>",
      "<br>",
      "<br>Raise plugin state: <a href=\"#raise=transpose.Chromatic\">transpose.Chromatic</a>",
      "<br>Raise plugin state: <a href=\"#raise=fill.SingleNotesScale\">fill.SingleNotesScale</a>",
      "<br>Raise plugin state: <a href=\"#raise=arpeggio.NamedNotes-AllHighlight-Positions\">arpeggio.NamedNotes-AllHighlight-Positions</a>"
    ]
  },
